==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|skīnanan|lang=ang}}, from an Indo-European root ''*skai-, *ski-''. Cognate with Old High German ''skīnan'' (German ''[[scheinen]]''), Old Saxon ''skīnan'' (Dutch ''[[schijnen]]''), Old Norse ''[[skína]]'' (Swedish ''[[skina]]''), Gothic {{Goth|[[𐍃𐌺𐌴𐌹𐌽𐌰𐌽]]}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of Ancient Greek {{term|lang=grc|σκιά}}, Old Slavic ''sěn’'' (Russian {{Cyrl|[[сень]]}}).

